_margins":true,"_score_margins":51.4,"_gate_fund_growth":0.2821438404763737,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":100.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02189272404840753,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":35.4,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.018066587210149643,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":72.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00044815415075388613,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":99.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.043730002,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":29.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":["paper"],"description_full":"Cencora, Inc. sources and distributes pharmaceutical products in the United States and internationally. The company's U.S. Healthcare Solutions segment distributes brand-name and generic pharmaceuticals, over-the-counter healthcare products, home healthcare supplies and equipment, and related services to acute care hospitals and health systems, independent and chain retail pharmacies, mail order pharmacies, medical clinics, long-term care and alternate site pharmacies, and other customers; distributes plasma and other blood products, injectable pharmaceuticals, vaccines, and other specialty pharmaceutical products; provides pharmacy management, staffing, and other consulting services; supply management software to retail and institutional healthcare providers; packaging solutions to institutional and retail healthcare providers; clinical trial support, product post-approval, and commercialization support services; data analytics, outcomes research, and other services for biotechnology and pharmaceutical manufacturers; pharmaceuticals, vaccines, parasiticides, diagnostics, micro feed ingredients, and other products to the companion animal and production animal markets; sales force services to manufacturers; and offers other services to physicians who specialize in various disease states, such as oncology, as well as to other healthcare providers, including hospitals and dialysis clinics. Its International Healthcare Solutions segment provides international pharmaceutical wholesale and related service, and global commercialization services; distributes pharmaceuticals, other healthcare products, and related services to pharmacies, doctors, health centers, and hospitals; and offers specialty transportation and logistics services for the biopharmaceutical industry. The company was formerly known as AmerisourceBergen Corporation and changed its name to Cencora, Inc. in August 2023. Cencora, Inc. was founded in 1871 and is headquartered in Conshohocken, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Robert P. Mauch Ph.D., PharmD | President, CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $6.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Cencora, Inc. is a large-cap healthcare business with a $67.5B market cap on $337.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 56% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 48-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 3% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $3.9B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.37\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 7.7\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 4.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Healthcare peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 28% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading at a 39% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","24 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Financial quality scores above most Healthcare peers","Healthcare sector 